1
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:12,666
A killer. A cop. Someone's... buried alive.

2
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:19,333
Oxygen is a crime, drama, mystery film directed by Richard Shepard.

3
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
When housewife Frances Hannon is abducted and buried alive,
detective Madeline Foster is brought in.

4
00:20:26,666 --> 00:20:32,666
With only 24 hours before Frances' oxygen runs out, Madeline pursues the
trail laid by a killer calling himself Harry Houdini.

5
00:25:33,333 --> 00:25:39,333
After capturing him, Madeline brings Harry back to the police station, but
is unable to get him to confess where Frances is buried.

6
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
As time runs down, Harry gets inside the head of unstable, alcoholic Madeline.

7
00:35:46,666 --> 00:35:52,666
Det. Madeline Foster, played by Maura Tierney.

8
00:40:53,333 --> 00:40:59,333
Harry, played by Adrien Brody.

9
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Clark Hannon, played by James Naughton.

10
00:51:06,666 --> 00:51:12,666
Frances Hannon, played by Laila Robins.

11
00:56:13,333 --> 00:56:19,333
Tim, played by Terry Kinney.

12
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
Jesse, played by Paul Calderon.

13
01:06:26,666 --> 01:06:32,666
Oxygen is a 1999 thriller film, directed and written by Richard Shepard.

14
01:11:33,333 --> 01:11:39,333
The film follows a troubled cop, Madeline Foster (Maura Tierney) as she
pursues a kidnapper who calls himself Harry Houdini (Adrien Brody).

15
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
The film was shot on location in New York City.

16
01:21:46,666 --> 01:21:52,666
The film explores themes of new york city, death
penalty, miami, florida, ransom, kidnapping.

17
01:26:53,333 --> 01:26:59,333
The tone is intense and emotional and mind_bending.
